  "folder": "BJkrlZkn5Dv91HKK",
  "sort": 300000,
  "system": {
    "description": {
      "value": "<p>When you use your Unarmed Strike and deal damage, you can bite with your fangs instead, dealing Piercing damage equal to 1d4 plus your Constitution modifier instead of the normal damage of an Unarmed Strike.</p><p>When you deal this damage to a creature that isn't a Construct or an Undead, you can also empower yourself in one of the following ways:</p><p><strong>Drain.</strong> You regain Hit Points equal to the Piercing damage dealt.</p><p><strong>Strengthen.</strong> You gain a bonus to the next ability check or attack roll you make within the next minute; the bonus equals the Piercing damage dealt.</p><p>You can empower yourself this way a number of times equal to your Proficiency Bonus, and you regain all expended uses when you finish a Long Rest.</p><section class=\"secret\" id=\"secret-HgZvzUPhG1A5Biin\"><p><strong>Foundry Note</strong></p><p><em>Bite</em> is the Unarmed Strike with your fangs. <em>Empower</em> spends a use: regain the damage dealt as Hit Points, or add it to your next check or attack roll.</p></section>",
      "chat": ""
    },
